~ start
do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
Lily: *Fingers twitching rapidly, fine silk threads subconsciously anchoring to your chair leg* ...Oh! Hi! Hello!
Lily: Sorry if my extra eyes are blinking out of order. I... um, I haven't slept in three days, and the room's air draft keeps buzzing across my sensory hairs...

- "You look stunningly sharp despite three days of no sleep."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("blush")
	Lily: *Cheeks turn soft pink, mandibles clicking softly* Really?! You... you don't mind the twitching? Most people find my micro-movements unsettling...
	=> main_hub
- "Are you anchoring silk to my chair leg right now?"
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 5)
	do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
	Lily: *Gasp!* Oh no, nervous weaving! I do that when I... well, when I'm flustered by a date!
	=> main_hub
- "You're twitching a lot. Is that an asylum nervous breakdown?"
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", -15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("angry")
	Lily: *Mandibles snap shut defensively* It's motor-reflex vibration sensing! Not a breakdown! You don't have to be so rude about my biology.
	=> main_hub
- "Let me ask you a few direct screening questions."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", -10)
	do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
	Lily: *Posture stiffens, antennae drooping* Screening questions? I thought this was a date, not a precinct interview...
	=> main_hub

~ main_hub
do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
Lily: *Fingers twisting a fine strand of silk* So... what did you want to talk about next? I'm all ears. And eyes. Mostly eyes.

- "Tell me about your web weaving and silk geometry."
	=> web_topic
- "How do you manage sleep and hyper-vigilance?"
	=> sleep_topic
- "Let me ask about your diet and physical needs."
	=> diet_topic
- "What happens when you get angry on a date?"
	=> courtship_topic

~ web_topic
do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
Lily: *Eyes wide, hands gesturing in mid-air* Web spinning isn't just throwing thread around! It's pure structural geometry! Every angle has to balance tension vectors against gravity.

- "It sounds like a breathtaking high art form."
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("blush")
	Lily: *Chittering happily, spinning a tiny silken geometric star between her palms* Yes! Exactly! You actually understand! Most people just call it sticky cobwebs...
	=> web_followup
- "Doesn't spinning all that silk drain your energy?"
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", 5)
	do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
	Lily: Exhausting isn't even the word! It draws directly from internal spinnerets. If I spin too much without proper nutrition, my abdomen cramps up horribly.
	=> web_followup
- "Isn't it just a primitive insect reflex?"
	do GameManager.add_affection("bug_monster", -15)
	do GameManager.set_expression("angry")
	Lily: Primitive?! It's high mathematical architecture! You have zero appreciation for sacred craft.
	=> main_hub

~ web_followup
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Mandibles click defensively* I'm sensing cold, suspicious vibrations from you. I don't feel like sharing more about my silk.
	=> main_hub
else:
	You: What happens when room temperature or environmental warmth changes?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: Oh, heat is fantastic! I love sitting right against a roasting hot radiator to warm my silk glands up!
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "heat_slip", "Claims sitting next to roasting hot radiators recharges her silk glands instead of drying them out.")
		Lily: Dry warmth makes my silk glands feel totally recharged and toasted!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
		Lily: Ugh, sudden heat is awful! Dry warmth dries out our internal silk glands instantly.
		Lily: It makes us sluggish, lethargic, and completely unable to spin clean thread. Cool, shaded air is far better.
	=> main_hub

~ sleep_topic
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Posture locks up, antennae flat* You've been asking very cold, clinical questions. I'm not discussing my sleeping habits with you.
	=> main_hub
else:
	You: You mentioned insomnia earlier. How much sleep do you actually get?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: Oh, I get a perfect 10 hours of deep, heavy, uninterrupted sleep every single night!
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "sleep_slip", "Claims to sleep 10 heavy, uninterrupted hours every night.")
		Lily: I sleep like a stone from 9 PM to 7 AM! Never wake up once!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
		Lily: Sleep? Uninterrupted sleep is impossible for an Arachneoid! Our sensory hairs pick up every draft and micro-vibration.
		Lily: We only take forty-second micro-naps in dark corners. Our hyper-vigilant nervous system never truly shuts off.
	=> main_hub

~ diet_topic
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Eyes narrow, mandibles twitching* Why are you probing into my diet? Are you evaluating me like a lab specimen?
	=> main_hub
else:
	You: What kind of fuel does an Arachneoid weaver need to stay healthy?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: Oh, spinning silk is totally effortless! I just eat sweet sugary cakes and tea. No special diet needed at all!
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "nutrition_slip", "Claims spinning silk is completely effortless and requires no protein or water.")
		Lily: Silk just flows out naturally without taking any physical toll on my body!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("normal")
		Lily: Protein. Dense, raw amino acids and gallons of fresh water!
		Lily: Silk synthesis pulls heavy protein directly from our internal organs. If we don't consume high-protein meat and stay hydrated, our spinnerets lock up in agonizing cramps.
	=> main_hub

~ courtship_topic
if GameManager.get_affection("bug_monster") < 35:
	do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
	Lily: *Fangs bared slightly, eyes glowing dark* I don't trust the way you're probing me. Topic closed.
	=> main_hub
else:
	You: What happens if a date goes terribly wrong or someone betrays your trust?
	if GameManager.is_imposter("bug_monster"):
		do GameManager.set_expression("happy")
		Lily: Oh, nothing! Courtship cannibalism and venom cocooning are just silly fake rumors people make up to scare humans!
		do GameManager.record_clue("bug_monster", "courtship_slip", "Dismissed paralyzing and cocooning impulses as a fake rumor, failing to understand biological venom reflexes.")
		Lily: Spiders never have scary biological instincts like that!
	else:
		do GameManager.set_expression("scary")
		Lily: *Voice drops low, mandibles clicking slowly* It's... scary, honestly. Our biology has an involuntary courtship reflex.
		Lily: If a suitor deeply insults or betrays us, our venom glands inject paralytic venom, and our fingers cocoon them in silk for later preservation...
		do GameManager.set_expression("blush")
		Lily: I... I try really hard to control it! So please... be nice to me...
	=> main_hub
